<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">1527 election in Cetin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1527</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The election in Cetin was the assembly of Croatian nobles held at Cetin Castle on 1 January 1527, after King Louis II died at Mohács. The nobles elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-i-holy-roman-emperor">Ferdinand of Habsburg</a> king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a> in return for promises of help against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>, beginning <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> rule over Croatia that lasted until 1918. Many Slavonian nobles chose his rival <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-zapolya">John Zápolya</a> instead.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/1527-election-in-cetin.jpg" alt="1527 election in Cetin" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Silverije · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cetingradski_sabor_1527.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
